{
  "name": "happy",
  "integration": "portainer",
  "description": "A Portainer server managing one Docker environment. Proves the whole default path: /api/endpoints is filtered to Docker-family Type values, /docker/info yields the host asset keyed on the daemon ID, /docker/containers/json?all=1 yields published ports as services on that host, and /docker/networks supplies the driver map that decides which container addresses are routable. The macvlan container becomes its own asset with a real LAN address and MAC; the two bridge containers do not, because 172.17.0.x and its derived 02:42:ac:11:00:x MAC are identical on every Docker host. Container and info bodies follow the examples in moby/moby api/swagger.yaml; endpoint fields follow portainer/api/portainer.go json tags.\n\nThe macvlan MAC in the payload is 02:42:c6:33:64:2a, which is how Docker derives a MAC from an address (02:42 followed by the four address bytes of 198.51.100.42). The asserted value is 00:42:c6:33:64:2a because the shared normalize_mac helper clears the locally administered bit, which every Docker-generated MAC carries. That is the correct treatment for an interface -- the platform normalizes a scanned MAC the same way, so the two still match -- and is why the MAC is never used in the foreign id.",

